# Build-context exclusions (audit 2026-07-16 · DOCKERIGN).
#
# The builder stage does `COPY . .`, so without this file the whole repo —
# including the entire `.git` history (which carries the deleted legacy PHP
# secrets for the life of the repo) and any stray local `.env*` — would be
# baked into the builder layer. Keep those out. Do NOT exclude Dockerfile,
# package.json/package-lock.json, prisma/, src/, public/, scripts/, or the
# tsconfig/next config files — the Dockerfile needs them.

# VCS history + metadata.
# NOTE: we exclude the git OBJECT database + reflog — that is where all committed
# blobs (current AND historical, incl. the deleted legacy PHP secrets) live, so
# this keeps the secret-bearing history out of the builder `COPY . .` layer. We
# deliberately KEEP `.git/HEAD`, `.git/refs`, and `.git/packed-refs` (tiny SHA
# pointers, no blob content) because the Dockerfile builder reads them to bake the
# deploy-identity SHA into `.build-info.json` (a blanket `.git` exclude would
# regress every deploy's SHA to "unknown"). Net: history out, HEAD pointer in.
.git/objects
.git/logs
.git/lfs
.gitignore
.github

# Installed / generated artifacts (rebuilt inside the image)
node_modules
.next
dist
coverage
.build-info.json

# Dead predecessor (removed from the tree; belt-and-suspenders)
legacy

# Docs + local-only compose
docs
docker-compose.dev.yml
.dockerignore

# Secrets / local env — must never enter the build context
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# Tests + fixtures (not needed at build/runtime; smaller context)
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/__tests__

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
